From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 07:12:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(particles): resolve server effects relative to their
 actor

Decode packet 118 as one reusable model that retains its unsigned
dimension, signed unique actor ID, float position, effect name, and
optional Molang JSON without rewriting typed nested values.

Bedrock 1.26.51.1 build 51061372 uses -1 for world-space effects. Its
client handler 14133fb50 drops effects from another dimension, ignores
missing attached actors, and passes attached positions to the bound
factory as offsets. Resolve standard Java particles from the tracked
actor's Java feet origin, then add the offset with float arithmetic.
This gives both direct and ViaProxy ordinary clients an initial
position; Java particle packets cannot retain an actor attachment.

The target's serializer 143aa8310 still writes a boolean before the
Molang JSON string. Versioned protocol schema metadata describes the
field differently, so preserve the executable's encoding. Native value
serialization 1421f9380/1421f9f70 uses an array of named typed values,
including recursive member_array objects. The model preserves those
bytes for native playback integration; the Java fallback cannot
interpret arbitrary custom graphs or Molang variables.

Verification executes 100 native serialization cases and 1600 native
handler admission cases with supplied stream, lookup, context-copy and
factory boundaries. Unit tests cover native field order, signed ID
limits, optional-field boundaries, nested JSON retention, missing
actors, and float-coordinate precision. Resource transport, native
emitter integration, interpolation and visible parity remain pending.
